From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adaptive: keep uniform decode graphs alongside varlen decode

Measured on PP6 (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, DSpark K=5, max_num_seqs=32, SM80):
with adaptive verification enabled but nothing actually trimmed, a step of
6 requests x 6 verification rows ran the 40-row graph, i.e. it did 11% more
verification work than the step asked for. Counting throughput dropped 12-15%
against the same build with the feature off, at unchanged acceptance (5.952 of 6)
and unchanged real row count (36).

Cause: CudaGraphManager._init_candidates treats the two decode capture strategies
as mutually exclusive. Under varlen_decode (set whenever the adaptive manager
exists) the uniform-decode branch is skipped entirely, so the only decode graphs
available are the varlen buckets, which are [1,2,4] + multiples of 8 - and 6x6=36
is not among them. Uniform steps whose row count is not also a multiple of 8 are
therefore padded up to the next bucket. Enabling the feature thus costs work even
on the steps it decides not to trim.

Fix: capture uniform decode graphs alongside the varlen set, skipping any row
count a varlen bucket already covers exactly (17 new graphs for this
configuration, 36 rows included). They are deliberately kept out of the
priority-ordered range partitioning: inserting them there would let a uniform
graph claim the row counts below its bucket and starve ragged steps of their
varlen graph, dropping those steps to eager. Instead each uniform descriptor is
prepended to the exact row counts it can serve, and _is_compatible() already
refuses a uniform graph unless the step really is uniform at that width, so a
ragged step still falls through to its varlen graph unchanged.

Signed-off-by: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
@@ -261,6 +261,12 @@
         capture_varlen_decode = (
             separate_decode_routine and bool(decode_mode) and self.varlen_decode
         )
+        # Uniform decode graphs are captured ALONGSIDE the varlen set rather than
+        # replaced by it. Varlen buckets are multiples of 8 above 8, so a
+        # full-budget step of 6 reqs x 6 rows = 36 has no 36-row graph and pads
+        # up to 40, verifying 11% more rows than the step asked for - on a step
+        # where adaptive verification trimmed nothing at all.
+        uniform_decode_descs: list[BatchExecutionDescriptor] = []
         for num_tokens, num_active_loras in product(
             capture_sizes, self.lora_capture_cases
         ):
@@ -275,9 +281,9 @@
                     num_active_loras=num_active_loras,
                 )
                 descs_by_mode[decode_mode].append(desc)
-            # Capture uniform decode specfifc graphs if required
+            # Capture uniform decode specific graphs if required
             #  (i.e. separate decode routine)
-            elif separate_decode_routine and decode_mode and not self.varlen_decode:
+            elif separate_decode_routine and decode_mode:
                 for decode_query_len in decode_query_lens:
                     rounded_num_tokens = round_up(num_tokens, decode_query_len)
                     rounded_num_reqs = rounded_num_tokens // decode_query_len
@@ -298,7 +304,17 @@
                     )
 
                     # avoid duplicate graphs
-                    if desc not in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]:
+                    if capture_varlen_decode:
+                        # A varlen graph of the same row count already serves a
+                        # uniform step with zero padding, so only the row counts
+                        # that would otherwise be rounded up need a uniform graph.
+                        if (
+                            rounded_num_tokens
+                            not in {d.num_tokens for d in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]}
+                            and desc not in uniform_decode_descs
+                        ):
+                            uniform_decode_descs.append(desc)
+                    elif desc not in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]:
                         descs_by_mode[decode_mode].append(desc)
 
             # recoverSSM cannot capture a dummy query wider than its workspace.
@@ -326,6 +342,26 @@
             descs.sort(key=lambda d: d.num_tokens, reverse=True)
             self._capture_descs[mode] = descs
 
+        if uniform_decode_descs:
+            # Capture them, but deliberately keep them out of the range
+            # partitioning below-built list: inserting them there would let a
+            # uniform graph claim the row counts under its bucket and starve
+            # ragged steps of their varlen graph (falling back to eager). They
+            # are instead prepended to the exact row counts they can serve, and
+            # _is_compatible() only matches a uniform graph when the step really
+            # is uniform at that width.
+            captured = self._capture_descs[decode_mode]
+            captured.extend(uniform_decode_descs)
+            captured.sort(key=lambda d: d.num_tokens, reverse=True)
+            for desc in uniform_decode_descs:
+                width = desc.uniform_token_count
+                assert width is not None
+                for rows in range(width, desc.num_tokens + 1, width):
+                    key = (rows, desc.num_active_loras)
+                    candidates = self._candidates.setdefault(key, [])
+                    if desc not in candidates:
+                        candidates.insert(0, desc)
+
         for mode in (CUDAGraphMode.FULL, CUDAGraphMode.PIECEWISE):
             mode_descs = tuple(reversed(descs_by_mode.get(mode, [])))
             for num_active_loras in self.lora_capture_cases:
